6.  ONNX Export and Inference

Convert trained Keras models to ONNX for deployment flexibility.

Scenario: Convert the trained dense model and run inference using the ONNX runtime.

a. Convert Keras Model to ONNX:

Use the `convert` command on the trained Keras model file.

sygnals-nn convert  
\--keras-model simple\_dense\_model.keras  
\--output-onnx simple\_dense\_model.onnx

  * `--keras-model`: Path to the input `.keras` file.
  * `--output-onnx`: Path to save the output `.onnx` file.
  * The tool attempts to infer the input signature automatically. If it fails, you might need `--input-signature '[tf.TensorSpec(shape=(None, 2), dtype=tf.float32)]'`.

b. Run Inference using ONNX Model:

Use the `run` command, pointing the `--model` argument to the `.onnx` file.

sygnals-nn run  
\--model simple\_dense\_model.onnx  
\--input-data data\_infer.csv  
\--input-cols "feature\_A,feature\_B"  
\--output predictions\_onnx.csv

  * The `run` command detects the `.onnx` extension and uses the ONNX runtime (if available) for inference.
  * Preprocessing (if needed) works the same way as with Keras models, using `--preprocessor-path`.

